    "text": "A finite group G is called conjugacy-expansive if for every normal subset N\nand conjugacy class C of G the normal set N C contains at least as many conjugacy\nclasses of G as N does. Is it true that every finite simple group is conjugacy-expansive?\n                                                   M. Bezerra, Z. Halasi, A. Maróti, S. Sidki",
